# Objective
Write the SQL migration files to create the babies table.

The idea behind the SQL migration files is that you essentially can version control the changes that you make to your db.
- up will be the applied changes, or "migration"
- down will undo those changes

This way db changes are traced and repeatable.

The babies table is constructed as such:
- id (uuid) PK - unique id to identify a baby. UUID can be automatically created using the pgcrypto extension's gen_random_id() to provide the default 
- full_name (TEXT) - name of baby, required via NOT NULL
- birth_date (DATE) - optional 
- created_at (TIMESTAMPTZ) - created date for the record. default value is the current time stamp

the general structure of the create statement here is 
CREATE TABLE [IF NOT EXISTS] table_name (
    col_name col_type column_constraints
    ....
)
